# Tailwind Class Order

When writing or editing `className`, `class`, or `cn()` arguments, order utility classes in this sequence:

1. **Size & position** — dimensions, spacing, positioning, stacking, overflow
2. **Color** — background, text, fill, stroke, gradients, opacity
3. **Border** — border, outline, ring, divide
4. **Rounding** — `rounded-*`
5. **Shadow** — `shadow-*`
6. **Children (flex & grid)** — display, flex/grid layout, alignment, gap, order

Separate groups with a single space. Keep variant prefixes (`hover:`, `md:`, `dark:`) attached to each utility.

## Group Reference

| Group | Examples |
|-------|----------|
| Size & position | `w-*`, `h-*`, `min-*`, `max-*`, `size-*`, `p-*`, `m-*`, `inset-*`, `top-*`, `relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`, `sticky`, `z-*`, `overflow-*`, `aspect-*` |
| Color | `bg-*`, `text-*`, `fill-*`, `stroke-*`, `from-*`, `to-*`, `via-*`, `opacity-*` |
| Border | `border`, `border-*`, `outline-*`, `ring-*`, `divide-*` |
| Rounding | `rounded-*` |
| Shadow | `shadow-*` |
| Children | `flex`, `grid`, `inline-flex`, `flex-*`, `grid-*`, `gap-*`, `items-*`, `justify-*`, `content-*`, `self-*`, `place-*`, `order-*`, `col-*`, `row-*`, `space-x-*`, `space-y-*` |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — groups mixed
<div className="flex gap-4 bg-muted p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-sm w-full border" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="w-full p-4 bg-muted text-sm border rounded-lg shadow-sm flex gap-4" />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="items-center justify-center hover:bg-primary flex h-9 px-4 rounded-md border bg-background shadow-xs" />

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="h-9 px-4 bg-background hover:bg-primary border rounded-md shadow-xs flex items-center justify-center" />
```

When refactoring existing classes, reorder to match this sequence without changing behavior.
